      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sent https://r.android.com/2169945 to delete (1)\n\nOn second though, moving the `defer` would mess up the order of logging (would see \"shutting down\" -\u003e \"Failed with ...\")\n\n\u003e I think we don\u0027t see (3) because it is written to stderr rather than logcat.\n\nAh, right. I\u0027ll leave that alone then. If we didn\u0027t want the stderr log, we could return a `std::process::ExitCode::FAILURE` from main instead of using `std::process::exit(1)` so that the `defer` runs properly, but it seems minor.\n\nRelated discussion: if the shutdown on exit is really important, then we should probably use a different technique. If this is compiled with `panic\u003dabort`, then it won\u0027t get run on any panic. Also, the usual unix stuff like unhandled signals will skip it.",
